{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbeddingGL","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbeddingGL","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedding","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":56,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.heckeActionGL_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.heckeActionGL_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":703,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L703-L706","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.heckeActionGL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.heckeActionGL","kind":"def","line":655,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L655-L701","doc":"**The Hecke action.** `H_{m+1}(q) → End(V^{⊗(m+1)})`, sending the balanced generator\n`σ_a` to the braiding of strand `a`.\n\nAll three obligations are discharged by the general-`n` relations above: the quadratic by\n`isHeckeGenerator_braidAt`, the braid relation by `braidAt_braid`, far commutation by\n`braidAt_commute`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.strandBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.strandBraid","kind":"def","line":647,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L647-L650","doc":"The braiding of strand `a`: `Ř` acting at sites `a` and `a+1` of `V^{⊗(m+1)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt_braid","kind":"theorem","line":623,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L623-L634","doc":"**The braid relation at general `n`.** `Ř_{ij} Ř_{jk} Ř_{ij} = Ř_{jk} Ř_{ij} Ř_{jk}` for\nthree distinct sites — `yangBaxter` transported through the three-site embedding, with no\nnew matrix computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_eq_embedTriple_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_eq_embedTriple_right","kind":"theorem","line":600,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L600-L621","doc":"`Ř` at sites `j, k` is `1 ⊗ Ř` at sites `i, j, k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_eq_embedTriple_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_eq_embedTriple_left","kind":"theorem","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L577-L598","doc":"`Ř` at sites `i, j` is `Ř ⊗ 1` at sites `i, j, k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_mul","kind":"theorem","line":560,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L560-L573","doc":"**The three-site embedding is multiplicative.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_update_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_update_apply","kind":"theorem","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L547-L558","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_apply_update","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_apply_update","kind":"theorem","line":539,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L539-L545","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.sum_collapse3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.sum_collapse3","kind":"theorem","line":506,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L506-L518","doc":"The three-site collapse: `2^n` terms become `8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.tripleEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.tripleEquiv","kind":"def","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L477-L504","doc":"The three free sites parametrise the states agreeing with `a` elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple_apply","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L469-L473","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedTriple","kind":"def","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L461-L467","doc":"A three-site operator acting at `i`, `j`, `k` and trivially elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt_commute","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L446-L450","doc":"**The braidings at disjoint site pairs commute** — far commutation for `Ř` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_commute","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L433-L444","doc":"**Far commutation.** Braidings at disjoint pairs of sites commute, at any `n`. This is\nthe defining relation `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `|i − j| ≥ 2`, in the site-indexed model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L369-L373","doc":"And satisfies the skein relation `Ř_{ij} − Ř_{ij}⁻¹ = q − qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.isUnit_braidAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.isUnit_braidAt","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L365-L367","doc":"Consequently the braiding at any two sites of `V^{⊗n}` is invertible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.isHeckeGenerator_braidAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.isHeckeGenerator_braidAt","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L357-L363","doc":"**The general-`n` result.** At any number of tensor factors and any two distinct sites,\nthe embedded R-matrix is a §7a Hecke generator: `Ř_{ij}² = (q − qi) Ř_{ij} + 1`. So it is\ninvertible, satisfies the skein relation, and factors with eigenvalues `q` and `−qi` — all\ninherited through `embedPairHom` at no extra cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.braidAt","kind":"def","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L353-L355","doc":"**The braiding at two sites of `V^{⊗n}`.** For any `n` and any two distinct sites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPairHom_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPairHom_apply","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L349-L351","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPairHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPairHom","kind":"def","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L338-L347","doc":"**`M ↦ M` at sites `i ≠ j` is an algebra map** `End(V ⊗ V) → End(V^{⊗n})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_algebraMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_algebraMap","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L332-L336","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_smul","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L326-L330","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_add","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L322-L324","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_one","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L304-L320","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_mul","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L289-L302","doc":"**The site-indexed embedding is multiplicative.** The `2^n`-term sum collapses to the\nfour assignments to the two sites, which is exactly the matrix product on the window. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_update_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_update_apply","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L277-L287","doc":"The embedded operator's entry from such a state to an arbitrary `b`: the off-window\ncondition is unchanged by the update, so it is `a`'s own condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_apply_update","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_apply_update","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L271-L275","doc":"The embedded operator's entry from `a` to a state differing only at the two sites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.sum_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.sum_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L241-L253","doc":"The collapse: a sum over all `2^n` states of a function supported on the states agreeing\nwith `a` off `{i, j}` is a sum over the four assignments to those two sites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.pairEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.pairEquiv","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L216-L239","doc":"**The two free sites parametrise the states agreeing with `a` elsewhere.** Fixing a\nreference state `a`, the assignments to sites `i ≠ j` biject with the states that agree with\n`a` off `{i, j}`. This is the one combinatorial fact the site-indexed calculus needs; every\nsum below collapses along it from `2^n` terms to `4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair_apply","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L211-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.embedPair","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L205-L209","doc":"A two-site operator acting at sites `i` and `j` of `V^{⊗n}` and trivially elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.yangBaxterN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.yangBaxterN","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorEmbeddingGL.lean#L183-L195","doc":"**The Yang–Baxter equation** `Ř₁Ř₂Ř₁ = Ř₂Ř₁Ř₂` on `(R^N)^{⊗3}`, every `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.c2_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedGL.c2_gt","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://gith